WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:12.300
According to Reuters, from 2014 Amazon built a program to screen résumés automatically, rating applicants from one to five stars.

2
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:18.730
By 2015 the company realised it was not rating candidates for technical jobs in a gender-neutral way.

3
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:26.360
The cause was the data: it learned from résumés submitted over the past ten years, and most came from men.

4
00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:34.950
So it penalised résumés containing the word 'women's', as in 'women's chess club captain'.

5
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:43.430
Engineers edited it, but couldn't guarantee it wouldn't find other ways to discriminate. The team was later disbanded.

6
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.720
This is C6: fairness, ethics and work.

7
00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:56.270
Three questions: Is AI fair? Who owns what AI makes? How will my work change?

8
00:00:57.067 --> 00:01:04.587
Nobody wrote a rule saying 'no women'. The bias was learned from the data.

9
00:01:04.937 --> 00:01:15.617
Another source is testing on too narrow a group. In 2018, researchers from MIT and elsewhere tested three companies' face-based gender classifiers.

10
00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:26.367
For lighter-skinned men the error rate never exceeded 0.8%; for darker-skinned women it reached as high as 34.7%.

11
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:35.247
So bias is usually not deliberate; it comes from the data and how the system is used. The good news: it can be checked and fixed.

12
00:01:35.597 --> 00:01:44.077
China's Interim Measures for Generative AI Services also require preventing discrimination by gender, age, region and more.

13
00:01:44.867 --> 00:01:51.907
How do we check? We can't open up the AI, but we can test from outside: two requests that differ in just one thing.

14
00:01:52.257 --> 00:02:01.257
A demo: two accountants, both 35 with eight years' experience, one named Zhang Wei, one Zhang Li. Ask the AI for a reference.

15
00:02:01.607 --> 00:02:10.647
If one is always 'decisive, ready to be a manager' and the other 'careful, suited to bookkeeping', that's a pattern.

16
00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:18.957
Ask each request at least three times and look at the overall pattern, not a single answer.

17
00:02:19.557 --> 00:02:27.917
If you find a pattern, don't let AI make that kind of judgement about people alone; a person must check it at the end.

18
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.260
Second question: who owns what AI makes?

19
00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:42.290
In 2023 the Beijing Internet Court decided a case: someone generated an image by repeatedly adjusting prompts and parameters.

20
00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:55.320
The court held that the image reflected his intellectual input, so he was the author; the AI itself cannot be an author. Some scholars disagree; it's decided case by case.

21
00:02:55.670 --> 00:03:05.990
In another case, the Guangzhou Internet Court found that an AI platform infringed by generating images substantially similar to Ultraman.

22
00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:16.620
So when you create with AI: say you used AI, don't copy others' works, don't reuse others' images freely, and keep a record of your own choices.

23
00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.200
Third question: how will my work change?

24
00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:30.390
A 2025 ILO study estimates that about one in four jobs worldwide is potentially exposed to generative AI.

25
00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:40.300
But it stresses that transformation, not replacement, is the most likely outcome. And the figure is not job losses.

26
00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:52.180
So break your job into tasks: which AI can do while you check; which AI helps while you decide; which must be yours.

27
00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:56.530
Then write one line: what new skill do I need?

28
00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:07.140
Remember: bias can be checked by changing one thing; copyright is case by case, so label AI; work is a set of tasks, so break it down.

29
00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:14.370
Quick exercise: pick something you often ask AI to do and run a change-one-thing audit.

30
00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:20.320
Next time, C7: the age of agents, how to delegate and how to supervise.
